    "title": "<p><strong>Table&nbsp;2.04</strong> Immunohistochemical characteristics of breast papillary neoplasms</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Imported from 5th edition<br><br>This table is a modified version of a table that was published in the previous blue book We have reviewed it and sent it also to Megane Troxell and her colleagues of the papilloma chapter to review",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" border=\"0\" width=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.2pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"107\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Neoplasm</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 182.05pt; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-right: none; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"243\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Myoepithelial markers (e.g. p63, SMMHC, calponin)</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 180.7pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"241\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">High-molecular-weight cytokeratins (CK5/6, CK14)</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 180.75pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"241\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">ER and PR</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 103.2pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"138\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Other</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 1; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 92.25pt; border: none; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"123\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Papillary fronds</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.8pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"120\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Periphery of the lesion</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 2; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"107\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Intraductal papilloma</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 92.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"123\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Positive</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"120\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Positive</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 180.7pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"241\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Positive: myoepithelial cells, UDH (heterogeneous positivity)</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Negative: apocrine metaplasia</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 180.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"241\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Positive (heterogeneous): luminal cells, UDH</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Negative: apocrine metaplasia</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 103.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"138\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">n/a</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 3; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"107\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Papilloma with ADH or DCIS</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 92.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"123\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Positive in the papilloma; may be scant or absent in the ADH/DCIS component</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"120\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Positive</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 180.7pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"241\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Positive: myoepithelial cells, UDH (heterogeneous positivity)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Negative: apocrine metaplasia, ADH/DCIS</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 180.75pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"241\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Positive (strong and diffuse): ADH/DCIS</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Positive (heterogeneous): luminal cells, UDH</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Negative: apocrine metaplasia</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 103.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"138\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">n/a</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 4; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"107\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Papillary DCIS</strong><sup>a</sup></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 92.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"123\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Absent; attenuated layer in rare cases</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"120\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Positive</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 180.7pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"241\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Positive: myoepithelial cells</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Negative: neoplastic cell population</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 180.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"241\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Positive (strong and diffuse)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 103.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"138\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">n/a</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 5; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"107\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Encapsulated papillary carcinoma</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 92.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"123\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Absent</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"120\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Usually absent</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 180.7pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"241\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Negative in the neoplastic cell population</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 180.75pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"241\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Positive (strong and diffuse)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 103.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"138\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">n/a</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 6; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"107\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Solid papillary carcinoma in&nbsp;situ</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 92.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"123\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Absent</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"120\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Absent or positive</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 180.7pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"241\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Negative in the neoplastic cell population</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 180.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"241\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Positive (strong and diffuse)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 103.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"138\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Frequent synaptophysin and INSM1 expression; chromogranin may be positive</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 7; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"107\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Solid papillary carcinoma with invasion</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Invasive solid papillary carcinoma</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 92.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"123\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Absent</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"120\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Absent in the invasive component</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 180.7pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"241\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Negative in the neoplastic cell population</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 180.75pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"241\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Positive (strong and diffuse)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 103.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"138\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Frequent synaptophysin and INSM1 expression; chromogranin may be positive</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 8; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.2pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"107\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Invasive papillary carcinoma</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 92.25pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"123\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Absent</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.8pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"120\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Absent</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 180.7pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"241\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Negative in the neoplastic cell population</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 180.75pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"241\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Positive</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 103.2pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"138\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">n/a</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">ADH, atypical ductal hyperplasia; DCIS, ductal carcinoma in&nbsp;situ; n/a,&nbsp;not applicable; UDH, usual ductal hyperplasia.</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><sup>a</sup>High-grade lesions may show a different pattern of staining.</p>",
